Suspension of Access; Scheduled Downtime; Modifications.  Cohere may from time to time and in its discretion, without limiting any of its other rights or remedies at law or in equity, under this Agreement:
suspend or revoke Customer’s access to or use of the Cohere Products or  Services, at any time, for any reason, including:
for scheduled maintenance;
due to a Force Majeure;
if Customer is delinquent in its payment of Fees under Section 9;
if Cohere believes in good faith that Customer or any Permitted User has violated any provision of this Agreement or any other guidelines Cohere provides to Customer, including the Usage Policy or that are posted on the Website;
to address any emergency security concerns;
Customer’s use of the Cohere Products or ServicesI contrary to the related Documentation; or
if required to do so by a regulatory body or as a result of a change in applicable law;
temporarily suspend the availability of a Custom Model where Customer has not accessed such Custom Model for 24 consecutive hours, provided that Cohere will promptly restore Customer’s access to the Custom Model when Customer attempts to access the temporarily suspended Custom Model; and
make any Modifications to the Cohere API SaaS Services.

